            # ordinary C enums. Under -fshort-enums, select the smallest
            # target integer that can represent every enumerator. This mirrors
            # the observable ABI choice for the supported 8/16/32/64-bit
            # targets and remains conservative for empty enums.
            # Clang chooses an unsigned compatible type for a non-negative
            # ordinary C enum when that is sufficient, even when all named
            # values would also fit in signed char. A cast may subsequently
            # carry an unnamed value such as 255, so preserve that ABI choice.
            return sview("unsigned char", 0, -1) if minimum >= 0 and maximum <= 255
            return sview("unsigned short", 0, -1) if minimum >= 0 and maximum <= 65535
            return sview("unsigned int", 0, -1) if minimum >= 0 and maximum <= 4294967295
            return sview("signed char", 0, -1) if minimum >= -128 and maximum <= 127
            return sview("short", 0, -1) if minimum >= -32768 and maximum <= 32767
            return sview("int", 0, -1) if minimum >= -2147483648 and maximum <= 2147483647
